From ef3986b671fa0311b1afba34680ce5cd92778644 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 02:31:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix PlantTopology.tsx: make the flow diagram dark-mode aware
 (Design Audit Finding #1)

The entire node-color system (13 node kinds x bg/border/text/accent/lane)
and most of the canvas chrome (background rect, grid dots, connector lines,
divider labels, status dots) were hardcoded light-mode hex, unconnected to
the dark-mode CSS variables shipped in phase-2.3-dark-mode-toggle. With dark
mode on, this was the one screen still rendering as a bright light-mode
diagram floating on an otherwise dark page.

index.css: added a --topo-<kind>-{bg,border,text,lane} token set (root +
.dark), same hue per kind as the original hex, dark values remapped to a
dark tinted card + brighter border + light tinted text. Border/accent
lightness is capped at 58% in dark mode specifically because a few of these
values are also used as a solid fill under white badge text elsewhere in
the file -- go much past that and white-on-fill contrast starts failing.

PlantTopology.tsx:
- COLORS object now holds hsl(var(--topo-*)) references instead of hex, so
  every existing consumer site (~40+ fill/stroke/style usages) keeps working
  unchanged -- this was a token swap, not a rewrite.
- Added a withAlpha() helper and used it everywhere the code was previously
  hand-rolling transparency via hex alpha suffixes (c.border + '80', + 'aa',
  template-literal + '33') -- that trick silently breaks once the base color
  is a var() reference instead of a hex literal, so those 4 call sites
  needed real fixes, not just a find-and-replace.
- Remaining hardcoded hex swept to semantic tokens: pending/warning state
  -> --warn, inactive/disabled -> --muted / --muted-foreground, status dots
  -> --accent / --warn / --danger, canvas background -> --card (was a literal
  #ffffff rect -- the actual worst offender, since fixing only the node
  colors would have still left a solid white canvas behind them), grid dots
  / connector lines / dividers -> --border / --muted-foreground, WATER FLOW
  label -> --accent / --accent-soft (existing soft-pill pattern already used
  elsewhere in the app).
- bg-white on the canvas container swapped for bg-card to match.

Left alone: 3 remaining #fff instances (badge count text on an accent fill)
-- safe as-is given the 58%-capped accent lightness above; and #0003/#0002
drop-shadow alphas, which are fine unchanged in either mode.

Verified: tsc --noEmit (0 errors), eslint on the changed file (0 errors, 32
pre-existing any-type warnings untouched), vite build succeeds, and the
compiled CSS output contains both the light and dark --topo-* values.
